      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15342640" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G44990-MONOMER" textLabel="9-cis-epoxycarotenoid dioxygenase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q7XJM2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The |FRAME: AT2G44990 CCD7| gene is one of nine |FRAME: TAX-3702 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;| genes that encode carotenoid dioxygenases. The gene encodes a |FRAME: AT2G44990-MONOMER 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene 9&apos;,10&apos;-cleavage dioxygenase| that cleaves |FRAME: CPD-14646 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene| between positions 10&apos; and 9&apos;, an early reaction in the pathway leading to production of strigolactones |CITS: [22422982]|. As typical to genes involved in this pathway, mutants in CCD7 display a dramatic increase in lateral branching |CITS: [15268852]|. In an earlier work the protein was expressed in carotenoid-accumulating strains of &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt; and tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; with several of the most common plant carotenoids. It was reported that the recombinant protein catalyzes the specific 9&apos;-10&apos; cleavage of |FRAME: CPD1F-129 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene|, producing |FRAME: CPD-13368 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal| |CITS: [15342640]|. However, later work showed that the actual substrate for the enzyme is |FRAME: CPD-14646 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene| |CITS: [22422982]|. In that work, all other &amp;beta;-carotene isomers, including &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-, 13-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-, and 15-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-&amp;beta;-carotene, were not converted. Those results were reproduced using enzymes from |FRAME: TAX-3702 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;|, |FRAME: TAX-39947 &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt; Japonica Group| and |FRAME: TAX-3888 &lt;i&gt;Pisum sativum&lt;/i&gt;| |CITS: [22422982]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G44990-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G44990.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q7XJM2" />
